# Let the UI (running as 'synth', a member of 'video') set screen brightness.
#
# /sys/class/backlight/*/brightness is created root-owned 0644, so without this
# the brightness slider is visible but inert. A udev rule is the right tool here
# rather than a sudoers entry: brightness is dragged live, and shelling out to
# sudo per motion event would be absurd.
#
# Both the chgrp and the chmod are needed — group ownership alone doesn't grant
# write against a 0644 attribute.
#
# One `sh -c` rather than two RUN+= lines so the pair either both apply or
# neither does, and so PATH resolves chgrp/chmod wherever usrmerge put them.
SUBSYSTEM=="backlight", ACTION=="add", \
  RUN+="/bin/sh -c 'chgrp video /sys/class/backlight/%k/brightness && chmod g+w /sys/class/backlight/%k/brightness'"
